{"audit_findings": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "This ontology demonstrates strong structural modeling but suffers from critical EDIFACT semantic losses. The primary failures are: (1) Complete absence of qualifier distinctions that define EDIFACT semantics (NAD+BY vs NAD+SU are indistinguishable), (2) Missing ~40% of mandatory D96A INVOIC segments including UNH/UNT envelope controls, CUX currency, and FTX free text, (3) Flattening of context-dependent segments into generic classes that cannot enforce EANCOM business rules.",
  "completeness_score": 0.45,
  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "UNHSegment",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "Message Header (UNH) is MANDATORY in all EDIFACT messages per ISO 9735. Without it, the message cannot be validated as conformant D96A INVOIC. Must include S009 composite (message identifier) with 0065='INVOIC', 0", "owl_reviewed_length": 24413, "consultation_logged": true, "audits_remaining": 2}

