{"audit_findings": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "This ontology demonstrates sophisticated OWL modeling with reification patterns and proper disjointness axioms, but it fundamentally fails as a D96A EANCOM INVOIC representation. It captures ~20% of required EDIFACT segments, lacks all qualifier distinctions that define EDIFACT semantics, and conflates abstract business concepts with concrete segment structures. The model is philosophically sound but operationally incomplete for EDIFACT processing.",
  "completeness_score": 0.22,
  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "DTM_DocumentDate",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "DTM+137 (Document/Invoice Date) is MANDATORY in EANCOM. Current :date property on HeaderSection is unqualified and semantically void. Must model as distinct class with qualifier 137."
    },
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "DTM_DeliveryDate",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale":", "owl_reviewed_length": 18715, "consultation_logged": true, "audits_remaining": 1}

