{"audit_findings": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "This ontology demonstrates sophisticated OWL modeling with inverse properties and reification patterns, but it fundamentally fails as a D96A EANCOM INVOIC representation. It models abstract concepts (Organization, Role) rather than concrete EDIFACT segments with their qualifiers. Critical coverage is ~25% - missing 12+ mandatory segment types including MOA, DTM, RFF, LIN, QTY, PRI, TAX with proper qualifiers. The 'flattening error' is pervasive: NAD segments are not distinguished by qualifier (BY/SU/DP), no DTM qualifiers exist (137/35/11), and business rules are absent.",
  "completeness_score": 0.25,
  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "DTMSegment with Qualifier Subclasses",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "MANDATORY. D96A INVOIC requires DTM+137 (Document/Message Date) as mandatory in header. The ontology has a", "owl_reviewed_length": 17306, "consultation_logged": true, "audits_remaining": 0}

